#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 840.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186158250} :activity/id #uuid "ecfe7472-c21f-5cb6-9a9a-8377a10cac54" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049786 :topic/id #uuid "13ff200a-f3dd-575f-8362-6dc70510c750" :topic/math-academy-id 2988} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186158250 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186158539 :tutorial/content "The **variance** of a continuous random variable is the expected squared difference between the variable and its expected value.\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the variance is defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[(X-\\text{E}[X])^{2}] \\\\  & ={\\int }_{S}(x-\\text{E}[X])^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIn practice, though, it's easier to use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\textrm E [X^2] - \\textrm E[X]^2\n$$\n\n \n\nFor example, consider the continuous random variable $X$ with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{x}{4}, \\quad 1 < x < 3\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\textrm E[X]{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\cdot \\frac{x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{12}|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we compute $\\textrm E[X^2]{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{4}}{16}|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =5-{(\\frac{13}{6})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "24436a92-f030-567a-aa1c-938371716e3b" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4805 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "e48a5625-3306-5288-bda8-33105998d690" :step/math-academy-id 29831 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186158251}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186158251 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157369 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157189 :question/id #uuid "0a870e80-5a73-59d2-997f-bec2d9a947e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-7988"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "697e5bea-20b4-5de0-9992-7a67ee932809" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048747}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157992} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157994} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430389} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430392} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434815} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444791} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444792} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484200} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484276}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Continuous Random Variable Given a Two-Branch PDF"} :step/id #uuid "4892229b-e20c-58a7-a09b-56a62bb1e09e" :step/math-academy-id 29832 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186158252}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186158252 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157370 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157190 :question/id #uuid "77bbf810-ec26-5224-9d3e-62de3e0529fb" :question/math-academy-id "e-7990"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c834972a-1ed0-585c-803c-906fcea8cea8" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157993} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157995} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430390} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430391} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434814} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434816} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444790} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484240} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484272} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484298}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Continuous Random Variable Given a Three-Branch PDF"} :step/id #uuid "891a6678-f4fa-595a-b179-6c1d5207f1e4" :step/math-academy-id 29834}] :activity/title "Variance of Continuous Random Variables" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186157534}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444793} :activity/id #uuid "160005bb-8326-5a29-9efe-92a05d5628ea" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049786 :topic/id #uuid "13ff200a-f3dd-575f-8362-6dc70510c750" :topic/math-academy-id 2988} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444793 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444792 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5575a9f-2ab2-5d7f-a9f8-276caa836627" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444780} {:answer/id #uuid "d0832666-aa34-5722-9c73-1e8c1c1870ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444782} {:answer/id #uuid "dd759a9a-fce0-5c1b-a261-33cbdb2e7216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444784} {:answer/id #uuid "e1dfce71-5ec8-5a3c-bd1e-1e6fb3662f40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444785} {:answer/id #uuid "f8e19652-da47-5018-894c-72ff00f667d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444786}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444785} :answer-field/id #uuid "c501e9ae-0a39-5e88-9d3f-80627d2d0978" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e581a350-34fb-5bb6-8fc4-e9d06576ecf2" :question/math-academy-id "q-90531" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }x\\cdot \\frac{4}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{4}{3{x}^{3}})|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =2-{(\\frac{4}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3d3ca8a5-5e8c-5065-8776-a34522517e00" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444795}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444794 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444791 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e9efdb4-7f80-5918-beaf-297fded0d1a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444772} {:answer/id #uuid "32231228-53fe-53d5-bdc4-f2108fb66469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444774} {:answer/id #uuid "543d492f-4858-541f-821f-46b005347464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444775} {:answer/id #uuid "90be949d-ed37-5555-9606-534582ba1286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444779} {:answer/id #uuid "dc814aab-899d-5c15-be40-875f5ab22753" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444783}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444783} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0c7e56e-c625-533d-aa7a-794522008c4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444788}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "51c295b5-218d-536a-afb4-4f24a659df27" :question/math-academy-id "q-131168" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{20(x-1)}{{x}^{6}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }x\\cdot \\frac{20(x-1)}{{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{20x-20}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{20}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{20}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{20}{3{x}^{3}}+\\frac{5}{{x}^{4}}{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{20(x-1)}{{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{20x-20}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{20}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{20}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{20}{3{x}^{3}}{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}-{(\\frac{5}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "581089fb-ba1b-5011-b705-bf6aeed4884e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444797}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444795 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430391 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "441dd7e3-e030-5310-9ecb-7b67a3982bac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.98" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430370} {:answer/id #uuid "4f0b7271-9bb4-550c-b029-e79bed346a53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430374} {:answer/id #uuid "81542d0a-0fb0-50ab-9035-5794eba4e936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.43" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430380} {:answer/id #uuid "c9be22c8-e40d-5cc8-8a81-8a499de04f94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430382} {:answer/id #uuid "e9cd7562-368d-5fd1-be77-af5eda236982" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430383}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430374} :answer-field/id #uuid "49546c79-a4c5-5d04-8800-05585ba7aeb8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430386}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5874ecb6-66d6-5729-9147-ef1e0e5bab53" :question/math-academy-id "q-90539" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{17}{24},$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}, & 0<x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}, & 1\\le x, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}|}_{0}^{1}+{(-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}-{(\\frac{17}{24})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{143}{576} \\\\  & ≈0.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nrounded to $2$ decimal places."} :step/id #uuid "7003b13e-c8c5-5ff3-8c6f-c0164d0ecf2d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444794}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444796 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444790 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f169529-16b9-5970-b3fb-d0c797adbd00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444773} {:answer/id #uuid "5afefafb-20e1-5716-b02e-540539f314ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444776} {:answer/id #uuid "65707762-b12f-554d-aba1-2a960aba5f32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444777} {:answer/id #uuid "683e74a6-80ae-5bde-af5a-1ba88edd8aee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444778} {:answer/id #uuid "b772c7d7-0de6-57a8-9652-c7c648566917" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444781}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444781} :answer-field/id #uuid "2208588d-645c-5de7-972e-8974e29492ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444787}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "066a3d21-35aa-5e6a-8d2f-0980dd8ef30f" :question/math-academy-id "q-131263" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{5}{3},$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{3}, & 0<x<2 \\\\ \\frac{2(3-x)}{3},\\, & 2\\le x<3 \\\\ 0 & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{x}{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2(3-x)}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{6{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{4}}{12}|}_{0}^{2}+(\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{6}){|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}+(18-\\frac{27}{2})-(\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{11}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{6}-{(\\frac{5}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7c709c4d-931f-560c-b9a0-530b648f2ff4"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444797 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430390 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1204147e-9d6e-5e43-8474-be634d7db4f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430366} {:answer/id #uuid "1efa5566-7842-5b7d-abc6-3035b571fbef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430367} {:answer/id #uuid "4b1cc392-4060-5a10-aaea-a16a825992de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430373} {:answer/id #uuid "635dd8c1-f102-56ce-a2d5-2b936e82ad9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{72}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430376} {:answer/id #uuid "ee6aa4d5-c7a1-5ab9-8654-14774348fc7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430384}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430376} :answer-field/id #uuid "03117e06-c0a6-56f8-b0fb-52f9c75a1cf1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "572f0ee2-d90d-5ec7-a063-65cce5fd61fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-131262" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{5}{6},$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x}{2}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{8}|}_{0}^{1}+(-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}){|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}-{(\\frac{5}{6})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{72}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "933683ca-d2bd-5923-859c-87dfb8040fe3" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444796}}] :activity/title "Variance of Continuous Random Variables" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444771}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484344} :activity/id #uuid "f43dd96a-540d-5f5a-b773-e86347bdd398" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049786 :topic/id #uuid "13ff200a-f3dd-575f-8362-6dc70510c750" :topic/math-academy-id 2988} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484305 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484276 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14743a6d-89dc-51f1-be5f-651e9f9685f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483601} {:answer/id #uuid "b67a9aef-d76c-5bab-8625-14577b91fed1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483932} {:answer/id #uuid "b98a4eda-a7fb-5b36-a2ee-9c2bf3e3cb46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483938} {:answer/id #uuid "c1f044e2-04da-5e9c-8032-d7a4b80cff3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483949} {:answer/id #uuid "c3c18450-3d1d-5233-9103-20c6853cd571" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483952}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483601} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6f8a025-5440-5c77-830a-6386ff67bfed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ce424fe3-1289-5449-b3af-c9a36901436b" :question/math-academy-id "q-131166" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{3}{2},$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{4{x}^{3}},\\, & 1<x<3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{9}{4{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{9}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{9}{4}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{4}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{4}-\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0ecc0901-9e15-5cf0-8e30-1547d76a2b8f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484324}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484324 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484272 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c298589-687a-53b7-a2f6-711c8b3fc022" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483641} {:answer/id #uuid "3ed8eee1-36f5-552c-b95f-65eb970a734a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483685} {:answer/id #uuid "59e03d02-257a-5ba6-b196-538b39c66509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{63}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483734} {:answer/id #uuid "b279e53b-ef58-5c32-bfc7-abaacf3a829d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483923} {:answer/id #uuid "c5398c5f-3701-531a-9962-9d86c1e50901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483957}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483734} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc39d208-b352-55e6-ab15-3fec98ea96ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c369ac76-b620-5984-a1bf-927bb5bda8e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-131261" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{7}{8},$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{3(x-1)}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3(x-1)}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3x-3}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}|}_{0}^{1}+(-\\frac{3}{x}+\\frac{3}{2{x}^{2}}){|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+3-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}-{(\\frac{7}{8})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{63}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "5bca35c4-d7e1-599c-85b9-815775171cde"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484338 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484240 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "206cf90d-4f29-55ab-9819-01d8ca172f38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.74" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483619} {:answer/id #uuid "3f9e2311-3d05-5655-aec5-752bdfbf86b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.89" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483687} {:answer/id #uuid "7099a365-62d4-5172-aafe-41927474df4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5.50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483788} {:answer/id #uuid "cdf20927-1bb6-5558-9a95-f586e071ff7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2.11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483980} {:answer/id #uuid "db3da4ad-81ab-5111-a66e-0ed1cd8ee204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "30.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484003}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483687} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee0bda9f-4431-5acd-981b-83f88e146a0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484187}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7ae79777-cfeb-50b2-91fa-571641f41141" :question/math-academy-id "q-90564" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=1.9,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{3}, & 0<x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{8}, & 1\\le x<5, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{5}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot 2{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{5}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{6}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}+{\\frac{{x}^{3}}{24}|}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =5.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =5.5-{(1.9)}^{2} \\\\  & =1.89.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "aad7aa7a-b7fb-509a-8115-548c42717537" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484355}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484344 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484200 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "708884fe-c46f-510c-8336-9b1ff8d57dd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483787} {:answer/id #uuid "916cf1d3-9858-5e7a-bde5-ef0c01dfa40b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{43}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483869} {:answer/id #uuid "cc7730f4-2296-5da8-a7ec-104cd0811268" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483977} {:answer/id #uuid "de0ca903-22de-5647-90cb-d355eba5356b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484008} {:answer/id #uuid "f2bedab4-4484-581e-8c7f-86e59afba6ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484054}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483787} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9a9aeae-7475-58db-b6eb-574c342ffd6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484189}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "126e0a3b-1df5-561d-b629-66be47834dfa" :question/math-academy-id "q-90529" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-4,\\, & 2\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}x\\cdot (2x-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}(2{x}^{2}-4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}-2{x}^{2})|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot (2x-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}(2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{3})|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{43}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{43}{6}-{(\\frac{8}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b7f49b20-6bd7-50d7-9326-47e7905139df" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484338}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484355 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484298 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b2b313e-b6a7-568c-a875-f9db4ce39dcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483639} {:answer/id #uuid "325fa17b-54bd-5aa0-9e67-721dd15642fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483656} {:answer/id #uuid "5a881950-5b53-5733-8066-0e2b41f6af6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{39}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483738} {:answer/id #uuid "6d4e985e-cf6f-56bf-aaa1-935086b1d3e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483781} {:answer/id #uuid "f1f6ae5c-8838-54ee-bde6-979554af985b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{31}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484050}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483656} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6082ae9-a37f-5a6d-98af-d4b226bb7c29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484188}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fe9a9f2d-c658-56d3-a233-bcc579aed36f" :question/math-academy-id "q-107779" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=4$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x}{27}, & 0<x<3, \\\\ \\frac{9-x}{27}, & 3\\le x<9, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{9}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{9}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2x}{27}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{9}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{27}(9-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{27}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{9}\\frac{1}{27}(9{x}^{2}-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{4}}{54}|}_{0}^{3}+{\\frac{1}{27}(3{x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})|}_{3}^{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{81}{4}-\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{2}-{4}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "dc4fe466-4de3-5c80-8ce7-3c36ce3f07df" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484305}}] :activity/title "Variance of Continuous Random Variables" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483565}]}
